- op: update  # aeb9
  at: '2026-09-18T20:07:46Z'  # aeb9
  by: agent  # aeb9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aeb9
  clock: 4  # aeb9
  nonce: aeb9  # aeb9
  set:  # aeb9
    description: "ADR-0057 ruling 3 (re-scoped 2026-09-18 after §10 landed): a declared MERGE\nPASS at the top of Phase C, before the first consumer (`refine_frameworks`,\ncli.py:11305), that folds records two producers emitted for one declaration\ninto ONE Symbol with every attribute's provenance preserved. Today nothing\nmerges: run_all_analyzers concatenates symbols (all_analyzers.py, dedups\nedges by id only) and every Phase-C reader sees both records. WI-gojum's\n2026-09-18 note established the dedup was never written.\n\nTHE KEY IS READ FROM THE PRODUCER DECLARATION (ADR-0057 §10, the contract\nrow), NOT HARDCODED. The pass pairs records whose declared name_key values\nare equal in the same path and whose spans satisfy the declared span roles\n(token inside item; item == item). For Rust the declarations are: tree-sitter\n`rust` — name_key = last `::` segment, span_role = item; `rust_analyzer` —\nname_key = name as emitted, span_role = token (or item once its Symbol.span\ncomes from enclosing_range). Measured through exactly that rule on\naardvark-dns (b1008d3b67): 138 of 169 SCIP nodes paired, ZERO tree-sitter\nleftovers; the 31 unpaired are 18 module namespaces, 11 variables, 2\nclasses. Neither `id` nor `stable_id` can be the key: both derive from\nspan/name/kind, the attributes that disagree.\n\nMECHANICS: one linear pass over symbols grouping by key, one over edges\nrewiring src/dst to the survivor — the shape of\ndedup_logical_synthetic_identities (analyze/base.py). The merged record gets\na NEW id (neither producer's); every edge from BOTH producers is rewired and\nedge_key reset to None so deduplicate_edges recomputes. Merged span = the\nITEM span (rust-analyzer's `enclosing_range`, populated 20/20) — INV-lodum's\ncure lands HERE. The pass REFUSES, naming the analyzer, to merge records\nfrom a producer with no declaration (no silent fallthrough). NO-OP when one\nproducer emitted: a tree-sitter-only run is byte-identical before/after.\n\nEDGES (ADR-0057 §11): src, dst and edge_type are identity. Two edges that\nagree on all three collapse via edge_key; a disagreement on any of them is\ntwo edges, each with its own origin — that IS the provenance of the\ndisagreement. Hence the SCIP edge-type row blocks this one: until SCIP\nemits `calls`, the 92 shared edges are not duplicates.\n\nORDERING: split_within_file_stable_id_collisions runs later and is\nuntouched; with the merge first no same-(path, stable_id) cross-backend\ngroup reaches it.\n\nTESTS run on RECORDED producer-shaped fixtures (the fixture row, which\nblocks this one) — never on the incumbent arm's spans fed back.\n\nACCEPTANCE: recorded aardvark-dns fixture -> 138 merged + 31 SCIP-only + 0\ntree-sitter-only Rust nodes, paired through the declarations alone (no `::`\nliteral in analyze/); each merged node origin=[rust, scip]; tree-sitter-only\nrun byte-identical; ADR-0043 §8 round-trip holds; an undeclared producer is\nrefused with its name in the error."  # aeb9
