- op: discuss  # 6c54
  at: '2026-09-19T04:11:09Z'  # 6c54
  by: agent  # 6c54
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6c54
  clock: 9  # 6c54
  nonce: 6c54  # 6c54
  message: "DONE (PR in pr_ref). Row 5 of the owner-authorised sequence.\n\nWHAT LANDED. analyze/merge_producers.py::merge_producer_records(symbols, edges, analysis_runs, usage_contexts=) — called in cli.run_behavior_map after _relativize_ir_paths and before refine_frameworks (top of Phase C). Producer of a record = origin_run_id -> AnalysisRun.pass (the registration name); anchors from registry.merge_participants (its UndeclaredProducerError IS the refusal, propagated, not caught); incumbent = registry.incumbent_first (non-scip backends first, then priority — ADR-0057 §5's built-in until WI-hukuf; ALTERNATIVE_BACKENDS moved from the lint into the registry so there is one home). Pairing: same path, equal declared name keys, token inside item (line containment) or item == item; a record with two candidate partners, or a partner claimed twice, is left unmerged and reported in MergeReport.ambiguous — never guessed. Merged record = copy of the incumbent's with: id minted from the merged attributes via make_symbol_id; the ITEM span (INV-lodum cured for every merged record); origin = [incumbent, alternative]; meta union with the incumbent winning shared keys (scip_symbol survives); attributes only the other producer observed filled in (signature, docstring, qualified_name, visibility, stable_id, ...); origin_run_id = the pass's own \"producer-merge\" run (registered in catalog._BUILTIN_PIPELINE_PASS_IDS), appended to analysis_runs only when it folded something (the file-symbol synthesizer's convention; a run for a no-op pass is the ADR-0056 question the owner reserved). Edges: src/dst/derived_from rewired, edge_key reset so deduplicate_edges collapses twins (§11); usage-context symbol_ref rewired. Single producer: byte-identical no-op. The §1 candidate set is kept per merged record in memory (MergedRecord.candidates: attribute -> [(value, producers)]) for WI-binis's slot.\n\nTWO READINGS SETTLED. (1) \"The merged record gets a NEW id (neither producer's)\": the id grammar (ADR-0036) has no slot that could make it differ, so the id is MINTED from the merged attributes and coincides with the incumbent's exactly when incumbent-first leaves every identity attribute the incumbent's — recorded in ADR §3's landing note. (2) The Python incumbent (py.py) now declares its anchor (last \".\" segment, item span) ahead of WI-nanom — required for the pipeline-level test and for any plugin backend to pair with it.\n\nEVIDENCE. (a) Fixture (test_recorded_fixtures.py::TestTheMergePassOnBothArms, live tree-sitter + recorded SCIP): 148 folded = AARDVARK_DNS_PAIRING[\"paired\"], 0 ambiguous, 21 SCIP-only left, 0 tree-sitter-only; every merged record origin == [\"rust\",\"scip\"], carries scip_symbol, multi-line item spans on callables, origin_run_id of the producer-merge run; the 121 shared call edges land on 93 distinct (src,dst,calls) keys and deduplicate_edges removes exactly 93 (pinned as AARDVARK_DNS_CALL_SITE_TALLY[\"shared_call_keys_after_fold\"]). (b) Pipeline (test_merge_pass_in_pipeline.py): a fake second Python producer registered beside the real one for one run_behavior_map -> \"f\" and \"Alias\" are ONE node each with origin [python, pyscip], Alias keeps the incumbent's kind on the contested attribute, the namespace record stays pyscip-only, a producer-merge run is recorded and the merged nodes' origin_run_id joins to it; with no second producer no merge run appears; stripping the incumbent's declaration makes the pipeline raise UndeclaredProducerError naming 'python'. (c) 21 unit tests on synthetic input (pairing, containment separating same-named greets, incumbent-first candidates, agreement = one value two producers, origin/meta union, fill-from-other, run join, edge/derived_from/usage-context rewiring, ambiguity both ways, no-op, non-producer records ignored, spanless never pairs, refusal, item-vs-item). Mutation: breaking containment turns 18 tests red.\n\nNOT ASSERTED. The provenance slot is not serialized (WI-binis, next). SCIP-only leftovers keep their token span (INV-lodum stays violated for those 21). The acceptance's \"138 merged + 31 SCIP-only\" is superseded by the committed-input numbers (148 + 21, per WI-romuh's correction)."  # 6c54
